IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc31-forms-periods`
IMPORT `ccc31-forms-soira`

-- ccc31-tests-soira.l4 -- tests for ccc31-forms-soira.l4 (Forms 52, 53 and 54). Written by work/gen-soira-tests.py: the expected value of every
-- case is written by hand from the text of the Form (line numbers are those of R.S.C.-1985-c.-C-46.txt), before any run.
-- A period of N years after a day begins ON that day (ccc31-forms-periods, fork F16): five years from 1 January 2026 are 1 January 2026 to 31 December 2030.

§ `Form 52 -- Order To Comply with Sex Offender Information Registration Act (lines 19006-19014)`

§§ `The notice applies to the person (line 19006)`

-- Convicted of a designated offence (s 490.011(1) answers yes).
#ASSERT `form 52 the order applies to the person` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Found not criminally responsible.
#ASSERT `form 52 the order applies to the person` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Neither convicted nor found not criminally responsible.
#ASSERT `form 52 the order applies to the person` FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not a designated offence (the Form is silent for it): not covered.
#ASSERT `form 52 the order applies to the person` TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The answer of s 490.011(1) is not covered.
#ASSERT `form 52 the order applies to the person` TRUE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 1 (line 19007): report for the first time, "whenever required"`

#ASSERT `form 52 para 1 the person must report for the first time` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not required under the Act: "whenever required" is not met.
#ASSERT `form 52 para 1 the person must report for the first time` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Paragraph 2 (line 19008): the period, "or for life", and whether the person must report on a day`

-- Every seam answers that the order is not for life: the period of the years the notice states.
#ASSERT `form 52 para 2 the period for which the person must report` 5 (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST (`form 52 for a period of years` OF 5)
-- Seam 1 answers that the order is for life: for life.
#ASSERT `form 52 para 2 the period for which the person must report` 5 (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST `form 52 for life`
-- Seam 2 answers that the order is for life: for life.
#ASSERT `form 52 para 2 the period for which the person must report` 5 (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST `form 52 for life`
-- Seam 3 answers that the order is for life: for life.
#ASSERT `form 52 para 2 the period for which the person must report` 5 (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST `form 52 for life`
-- Seam 4 answers that the order is for life: for life.
#ASSERT `form 52 para 2 the period for which the person must report` 5 (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST `form 52 for life`
-- A seam answers NOTHING and none answers JUST TRUE: not covered.
#ASSERT `form 52 para 2 the period for which the person must report` 5 NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- One seam says life even though another is not covered: life.
#ASSERT `form 52 para 2 the period for which the person must report` 5 NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST `form 52 for life`
-- The first day of the period.
#ASSERT `form 52 para 2 the person must report on the day` (`form 52 for a period of years` OF 5) (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The last day of the period.
#ASSERT `form 52 para 2 the person must report on the day` (`form 52 for a period of years` OF 5) (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 31 12 2030) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The day after the period ends.
#ASSERT `form 52 para 2 the person must report on the day` (`form 52 for a period of years` OF 5) (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 1 1 2031) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A day before the period begins.
#ASSERT `form 52 para 2 the person must report on the day` (`form 52 for a period of years` OF 5) (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not required under section 4.1 or 4.3 of the Act that day: "whenever required" is not met.
#ASSERT `form 52 para 2 the person must report on the day` (`form 52 for a period of years` OF 5) (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 31 12 2030) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- For life: still required long after.
#ASSERT `form 52 para 2 the person must report on the day` `form 52 for life` (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 1 1 2031) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- For life, but not required under section 4.1 or 4.3 that day.
#ASSERT `form 52 para 2 the person must report on the day` `form 52 for life` (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2031) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- For life, but a day before the period begins.
#ASSERT `form 52 para 2 the person must report on the day` `form 52 for life` (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Paragraphs 3 and 4 (lines 19009-19010): information will be collected; information will be registered`

#ASSERT `form 52 para 3 information will be collected` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 52 para 3 information will be collected` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 52 para 4 information will be registered` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 52 para 4 information will be registered` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 5 (line 19011): "If you believe ... you may ask ... to correct the information"`

#ASSERT `form 52 para 5 the person may ask for a correction` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `form 52 para 5 the person may ask for a correction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE; the function is named for a power ("may ask") and its "if you believe" gate failed, which the name-test sweep answers NOTHING, not JUST FALSE; the person does not believe there is an error or omission
#ASSERT `form 52 para 5 the person may ask for a correction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 52 para 5 the person may ask for a correction` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 52 para 5 the person may ask for a correction` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 6 (line 19012): the right to apply to a court, and the right to appeal its decision`

#ASSERT `form 52 para 6 the person may apply to terminate the order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 52 para 6 the person may apply to terminate the order` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 52 para 6 the person may appeal the decision` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No decision of the court to appeal from yet.
#ASSERT `form 52 para 6 the person may appeal the decision` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 52 para 6 the person may appeal the decision` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 7 (line 19013): "If you are found to ... you may be subject to a fine or imprisonment, or to both"`

#ASSERT `form 52 para 7 the consequence of contravening the order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 52 para 7 the consequence of contravening the order` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Paragraph 8 (line 19014): "If you are found to ... you may be subject to a fine or imprisonment, or to both"`

#ASSERT `form 52 para 8 the consequence of providing false or misleading information` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 52 para 8 the consequence of providing false or misleading information` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Form 53 -- Notice of Obligation To Comply with Sex Offender Information Registration Act (lines 19024-19033)`

§§ `The notice applies to the person (line 19024)`

-- Convicted of an offence in the Code definition.
#ASSERT `form 53 the person is required to comply` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Convicted of an offence in the National Defence Act definition.
#ASSERT `form 53 the person is required to comply` TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Found not criminally responsible.
#ASSERT `form 53 the person is required to comply` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Neither convicted nor found not criminally responsible.
#ASSERT `form 53 the person is required to comply` FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- In neither definition: the Form is silent.
#ASSERT `form 53 the person is required to comply` TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 1 (line 19025): report for the first time, "whenever required"`

#ASSERT `form 53 para 1 the person must report for the first time` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not required under the Act: "whenever required" is not met.
#ASSERT `form 53 para 1 the person must report for the first time` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Paragraph 2 (line 19026): the period, "or for life", and whether the person must report on a day`

-- Every seam answers that the order is not for life: the period of the years the notice states.
#ASSERT `form 53 para 2 the period for which the person must report` 5 (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST (`form 53 for a period of years` OF 5)
-- Seam 1 answers that the order is for life: for life.
#ASSERT `form 53 para 2 the period for which the person must report` 5 (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST `form 53 for life`
-- Seam 2 answers that the order is for life: for life.
#ASSERT `form 53 para 2 the period for which the person must report` 5 (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST `form 53 for life`
-- A seam answers NOTHING and none answers JUST TRUE: not covered.
#ASSERT `form 53 para 2 the period for which the person must report` 5 NOTHING (JUST FALSE) FALSE 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- One seam says life even though another is not covered: life.
#ASSERT `form 53 para 2 the period for which the person must report` 5 NOTHING (JUST TRUE) FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST `form 53 for life`
-- A shorter period applies and is shorter (5 against 10 years): the shorter period.
#ASSERT `form 53 para 2 the period for which the person must report` 10 (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE 5 EQUALS JUST (`form 53 for a period of years` OF 5)
-- A shorter period applies but is not shorter (15 against 10 years): the years the notice states.
#ASSERT `form 53 para 2 the period for which the person must report` 10 (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE 15 EQUALS JUST (`form 53 for a period of years` OF 10)
-- No shorter period applies: the years the notice states.
#ASSERT `form 53 para 2 the period for which the person must report` 10 (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE 5 EQUALS JUST (`form 53 for a period of years` OF 10)
-- The first day of the period.
#ASSERT `form 53 para 2 the person must report on the day` (`form 53 for a period of years` OF 3) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The last day of the period.
#ASSERT `form 53 para 2 the person must report on the day` (`form 53 for a period of years` OF 3) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 28 2 2029) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The day after the period ends.
#ASSERT `form 53 para 2 the person must report on the day` (`form 53 for a period of years` OF 3) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 1 3 2029) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A day before the period begins.
#ASSERT `form 53 para 2 the person must report on the day` (`form 53 for a period of years` OF 3) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 28 2 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not required under section 4.1 or 4.3 of the Act that day: "whenever required" is not met.
#ASSERT `form 53 para 2 the person must report on the day` (`form 53 for a period of years` OF 3) (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 28 2 2029) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- For life: still required long after.
#ASSERT `form 53 para 2 the person must report on the day` `form 53 for life` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 1 3 2029) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- For life, but not required under section 4.1 or 4.3 that day.
#ASSERT `form 53 para 2 the person must report on the day` `form 53 for life` (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 3 2029) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- For life, but a day before the period begins.
#ASSERT `form 53 para 2 the person must report on the day` `form 53 for life` (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE (Date 28 2 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

